  "content": {
    "problemStatement": "You are given a positive integer NNN.\n\nConsider an array AAA of length NNN. Let PiP_iPi​ denote the sum of the first iii elements of AAA and SiS_iSi​ denote the sum of the last iii elements of AAA.\n\nYou need to construct the array AAA of size NNN such that all of the following conditions are met:\n\n\n−109≤Ai≤109-10^9 \\leq A_i \\leq 10^9−109≤Ai​≤109, for all (1≤i≤N)(1\\le i \\le N)(1≤i≤N)\nPi&gt;SiP_i \\gt S_iPi​&gt;Si​ if iii is odd, for each (1≤i&lt;N)(1 \\leq i \\lt N)(1≤i&lt;N)\nPi&lt;SiP_i \\lt S_iPi​&lt;Si​ if iii is even, for each (1≤i&lt;N)(1 \\leq i \\lt N)(1≤i&lt;N)\nIf there are multiple solutions, you can print any of them.\n\nIf there is no such array, print −1-1−1 instead.\n\n\nInput Format\n\nEach test contains multiple test cases. The first line contains the number of test cases TTT.\nThe only line of each test case contains a single integer NNN, where NNN is the length of the required array.\n\n\nOutput Format\nFor each test case, if a **valid** array exists, print NNN space-separated integers A1,A2,…,ANA_1, A_2, \\ldots, A_NA1​,A2​,…,AN​ satisfying all the given conditions.\n\n\nIf there are multiple solutions, you can print any of them.\n\nIf there is no such array, print −1-1−1 instead.",
    "constraints": [
      "1≤T≤1031 \\leq T \\leq 10^31≤T≤103",
      "2≤N≤1052 \\leq N \\leq 10^52≤N≤105",
      "The sum of NNN over all test cases won't exceed 3⋅1053 \\cdot 10^53⋅105."
    ],
    "inputFormat": "",
    "outputFormat": "",
    "notes": [],
    "sampleTestCases": [
      {
        "id": "sample_1",
        "type": "reg",
        "input": "3\n2\n3\n4",
        "output": "343 -343\n-1\n0 -5 343 -100",
        "explanation": "Explanation:\nTest case 111: All elements are in the given range for the array A=[343,−343]A = [343, -343]A=[343,−343].\n\nFor i=1i = 1i=1: Since iii is odd, P1=343P_1 = 343P1​=343 is greater than S1=−343S_1 = -343S1​=−343.\n\nTest case 222: It can be proved that no array of length 333 exists satisfying all conditions.\nTest case 333: All elements are in the given range for the array A=[0,−5,343,−100]A = [0, -5, 343, -100]A=[0,−5,343,−100].\n\nFor i=1i = 1i=1: Since iii is odd, P1=0P_1 = 0P1​=0 is greater than S1=−100S_1 = -100S1​=−100.\nFor i=2i = 2i=2: Since iii is even, P2=0+(−5)=−5P_2 = 0 + (-5) = -5P2​=0+(−5)=−5 is less than S2=343+(−100)=243S_2 = 343 + (-100) = 243S2​=343+(−100)=243.\nFor i=3i = 3i=3: Since iii is odd, P3=0+(−5)+343=338P_3 = 0 + (-5) + 343 = 338P3​=0+(−5)+343=338 is greater than S3=(−5)+343+(−100)=238S_3 = (-5)+343 +(-100) = 238S3​=(−5)+343+(−100)=238."
      }
    ]
